! Silicon in the diamond structure at a = 10.20 bohr -- the cell of QE's
! test-suite/pw_scf/scf.in -- for the X-ray structure factors.
!
! Two things differ from that input and both are convergence rather than
! physics: ecutwfc = 30 instead of 12, and an 8x8x8 k-grid instead of two
! k-points. The forbidden (222) reflection is a difference of two nearly equal
! atomic contributions, so it is the quantity here that converges last: it
! moves 0.352 -> 0.361 between 12 and 30 Ry and 0.361 -> 0.347 between 4x4x4
! and 8x8x8, and is stable in both by these values.
!
! The Elk reference for it is tests/data/elk/si-sfac.elk.in, the same cell and
! the same k-grid.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 2, celldm(1) = 10.20, nat = 2, ntyp = 1,
    ecutwfc = 30.0,
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Si  28.086  Si.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (alat)
 Si 0.00 0.00 0.00
 Si 0.25 0.25 0.25
K_POINTS {automatic}
 8 8 8 0 0 0
